    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "In 1984, the Australian doctor Barry Marshall was so sure that bacteria, not stress, caused most stomach ulcers that he drank a culture of them to prove it. He later shared a Nobel Prize."
    },
    {
     "text": "In chapter five of Suicidal Empathy, Gad Saad tells stories like these to make a point. In science, the consensus can be wrong, and the word settled should make us nervous."
    }
   ]
  },
