    {
     "id": "em",
     "type": "label",
     "x": 640,
     "y": 620,
     "text": "\"settled science\" as an appeal to emotion?",
     "color": "#ffb347",
     "d": 3.0,
     "in": 2
    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The philosopher Karl Popper argued that a scientific claim has to be falsifiable: there must be some result that could prove it wrong."
    },
    {
     "text": "That makes science humble by design. Every theory is the best one so far, never the final word."
    },
    {
     "text": "Saad's worry is that the phrase settled science is now used less as a summary of evidence, and more as an emotional appeal: if you question this, you must not care about people."
    }
   ]
  },
