     "color": "#c792ea",
     "d": 1.4,
     "size": 24,
     "in": 2
    }
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The psychologist Philip Tetlock describes taboo trade-offs: we refuse to weigh sacred values, like health or safety, against things like money or freedom, because even doing the sums feels monstrous."
    },
    {
     "text": "But every policy trades something for something else."
    },
    {
     "text": "As the economist Thomas Sowell put it, there are no solutions, only trade-offs."
    }
   ]
