   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "COVID is Saad's main example. Before vaccines, researchers estimated that the infection fatality rate for people under sixty was about three or four in ten thousand. For older people, it was many times higher."
    },
    {
     "text": "That steep age gradient, he argues, should have shaped policy: protect the vulnerable, and weigh the costs of closing schools and businesses for everyone else."
    }
   ]
