   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Saad's most heated example is gender medicine for young people."
    },
    {
     "text": "In 2024, England's Cass Review, a four-year independent study, concluded that the evidence for puberty blockers in children was remarkably weak."
    },
    {
     "text": "That same year, the New York Times reported that the American researcher Johanna Olson-Kennedy had not published results from a large federally funded study of puberty blockers, saying she worried they could be weaponized. The results reportedly showed no improvement in mental health."
    }
