   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Saad's critics say he picks the cases where the consensus wobbled, and skips the many where it held: vaccines, smoking and cancer, evolution itself."
    },
    {
     "text": "Questioning science is healthy. Treating every expert as a fraud isn't. Most of the time, the consensus is the best bet we have."
    },
    {
     "text": "Shared ground: science earns trust by showing its work, admitting mistakes, and letting people disagree out loud."
    }
